1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:26,000
In Aristotle's words, that which is in locomotion must arrive at the half-way stage before it arrives at the goal.

2
00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:56,000
So to run 100 metres, first run half of it. Then half of what's left, then half of that.

3
00:01:01,000 --> 00:01:26,000
The running totals are one half, three quarters, seven eighths, fifteen sixteenths, creeping towards the whole.

4
00:01:31,000 --> 00:01:56,000
After 10 halvings, you've run 1,023 parts in 1,024, and less than 10 centimetres is left.

5
00:02:01,000 --> 00:02:26,000
After 20, less than a tenth of a millimetre is left. But there is always a half still to run.

6
00:02:31,000 --> 00:02:56,000
There's a nastier version. Before the half-way mark, you must reach the quarter mark, and before that, the eighth.

7
00:03:01,000 --> 00:03:26,000
Then the run has no first step at all. So how does it ever begin?

8
00:03:31,000 --> 00:03:56,000
Aristotle noted that the Achilles is much the same argument. In our race, the gaps shrink by tenths, not halves.

9
00:04:01,000 --> 00:04:26,000
Zeno's arrow attacks motion from the other side, by cutting time into instants.

10
00:04:31,000 --> 00:04:56,000
Take an arrow in flight, and freeze a single instant.

11
00:05:01,000 --> 00:05:26,000
In that instant, it fills a space exactly its own size, so it isn't moving.

12
00:05:31,000 --> 00:05:56,000
But the whole flight is made of instants like this one. So when does the arrow move?

13
00:06:01,000 --> 00:06:26,000
Aristotle replied that time is not made of indivisible nows, any more than a line is made of points.

14
00:06:31,000 --> 00:06:56,000
The modern answer treats speed at an instant as a limit.

15
00:07:01,000 --> 00:07:26,000
Say it flies at 50 metres a second. In a tenth of a second, it goes 5 metres.

16
00:07:31,000 --> 00:07:56,000
In a hundredth, it goes half a metre. Distance over time stays at 50 metres a second, however short the interval.

17
00:08:01,000 --> 00:08:26,000
In a single instant it goes nowhere, and zero divided by zero isn't a number at all.

18
00:08:31,000 --> 00:08:56,000
So the speed at an instant is defined as that limit.

19
00:09:01,000 --> 00:09:26,000
On this view, motion doesn't happen inside an instant. It is being in different places at different times.

20
00:09:31,000 --> 00:09:56,000
The last of the four, the stadium, has rows of equal blocks passing each other in opposite directions.
